00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.000
$%&amp;!

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.000
Look, Mr. Carney, the question is not did you pick up the poker.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.000
We know you did.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.000
Your fingerprints are all over it in blood.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.000
It could be.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.000
I just don't remember anything I did.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:47.000
But you remember you didn't have a fight with Mr. Schuett.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.000
Kill him with the poker. You're certain about that.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.000
I told you I was.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.000
Carney.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.000
You're not helping us.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
I don't know what to tell you.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.000
I found him.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.000
About the time you came and he was dead.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.000
You could have let us in instead of running off.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.000
You have to understand.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
That was the act of a guilty man.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.000
You had no reason to think you weren't alone in the house with Mr. Schuett.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
What about enemies?

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:27.000
You ought to know if there were any people who might have wanted him out of the way.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.000
You've been living under the same roof with him for a long time.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
It's not the same roof.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.000
It was his house.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.000
It's not his house.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.000
It's not the same roof.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.000
It was his roof.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
Everything was his.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.000
He never let me forget.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.000
He never let you forget?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.000
My place.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
Like a prison.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.000
Why didn't you quit? There are plenty of jobs for good housemen.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.000
Just like betraying the skillet for the fire.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.000
People are all the same when you have to wait on them.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Why did you go back to that house last night?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.000
Because I...

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.000
I don't know.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.000
I chose to.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
All right, now.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.000
This fight at the hotel, what was that all about?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.000
Some crazy man knocked at the door,

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.000
and then he came at me.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.000
I don't know what I ever did to him.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.000
People.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.000
He didn't say why or what he was after?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:31.000
He didn't say anything.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Anything we can do for you?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
No.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.000
Any questions we can answer?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.000
No.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Yes?

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.000
Yes.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.000
How's...

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.000
How's Mr. McCalber?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:19.000
Your bird is well taken care of.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.000
Carney worked for old Horatio Shute for 20 years.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
He hated every minute of it, but he hung on.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.000
It bends your mind if you think about it.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:31.000
I am thinking about it.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.000
A great deal.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.000
You think you've got a fire, Chief?

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.000
I can see that.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.000
All right, let's get the fire extinguishers out of here

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.000
and back on the trucks.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Well, Chief, you missed all the fun.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.000
My office catches fire, and you call it fun?

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.000
No fire, just smoke.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.000
We have a smoke-free fire.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.000
I'm going to get the fire extinguisher.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.000
No fire, just smoke.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.000
We have a smoke-expeller operating.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.000
Have the office clear in about 10 minutes.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
I'll take that.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.000
Where did it land?

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.000
Over there. I'll show you.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Chemical reaction.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.000
And?

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.000
Model RL, rifle launch.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.000
No question, Chief.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.000
Came through the window.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.000
All right, thank you, Lieutenant.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.000
Mark, Ed,

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.000
I suppose we take a break in the park.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:09.000
Allie, we're going out for some fresh air.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.000
Now let's put this so-called fire together.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.000
See how it shapes.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.000
We open with a little bit of a twist.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.000
We open with a little bit of a twist.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.000
We open with a little bit of a twist.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.000
We open with a little bit of a twist.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.000
We open with Eve alone in the office.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.000
A call comes in from communications.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.000
I'm to report immediately to Commissioner Randall.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.000
Obviously, a plot to get you out of the office.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.000
Obviously, since the Commissioner knew nothing about it.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.000
From the time you left the office

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.000
to the arrival of the fire department...

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.000
Could only have been minutes, Chief.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.000
Yeah, but long enough.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
Yeah, for a bomb to fill the office with smoke.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.000
Why would any cat want to fake a fire?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
With a lot less trouble, you could have the real thing.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.000
Because this cat only wanted to get inside.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.000
No one could just walk in and out of there

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.000
with all those firemen swarming in.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.000
Could if he were masquerading as a fireman.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.000
Point is...

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.000
Point is, what was he after?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
The bird! Where is it?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.000
They blew it.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.000
Figured all the odds and still came up empty.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.000
The great Arnie Sims struck out?

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.000
How?

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.000
Doesn't matter how.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.000
We still don't have that crummy bird.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.000
You should have done like I said earlier.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Just gone in and swiped it.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.000
Waltz through a building full of cops

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.000
carrying a birdcage.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
Woo-hoo.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.000
Yeah, I'm Connie McKay.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.000
We'd like to ask a few questions.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.000
Sure, fire away.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:48.000
Mr. Alfred Carney says you sold him a bird.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.000
Carney.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.000
Hmm.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.000
Yeah, that name seems familiar.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:59.000
He's a suspect in Horatio Schubert's murder.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:02.000
Oh, yeah, I remember reading about that.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.000
The bird was an Indian hill miner.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.000
Yeah, yeah. Oh, sure.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
Yeah, talked up a storm.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.000
You can say that again.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.000
And again.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.000
We have reason to believe that someone else

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.000
was interested in that particular bird.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.000
Oh, yeah? Who's that?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.000
That's what we'd like to find out.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.000
Hmm.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.000
Well, uh...

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.000
Yeah, yeah, there was someone.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.000
A girl. A pretty girl.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.000
She didn't ask for that bird in particular,

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.000
but she got all shook up

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.000
when I told her I didn't have a talking mind.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
Thank you, Mr. McKay.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.000
Oh, well, you're entirely welcome, Chief.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Anytime, anything to help the police.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Oh, uh, Chief, uh...

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.000
I just happen to think, uh...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.000
I mean, under the circumstances and all,

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.000
do you think that Carney might be willing to sell him?

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.000
I mean, the bird, back to me?

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.000
No, I doubt that the owner would be interested.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.000
But I'd be glad to pass your proposition along to him.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.000
Oh, uh, thanks a lot.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:24.000
It looks as if our killer has an accomplice.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.000
A pretty girl.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:28.000
I've seen some weirdos,

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
but that guy McKay cops the cookies.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.000
Friendly enough?

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.000
And willing to help the police, despite his prison record?

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
I give up. How?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.000
How what?

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.000
How do you look at a guy and know that he's done time?

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.000
The way he spoke.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.000
He kept hiding his lips so we couldn't see them.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:51.000
Cons do that when they're supposed to be observing silent periods.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.000
Right. Uh-huh.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Thank you. Bye-bye.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.000
Well, the Chief was right.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:06.000
Don't look so surprised.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.000
In and out on three charges of larceny.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.000
Five years ago, according to his probation report,

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.000
he opened a pet shop.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.000
He's been clean ever since.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:16.000
Whistle for the doggy. Good for him.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.000
However, experience has taught me

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:21.000
to regard penitent sinners with a degree of caution.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:24.000
What did he do? He wants to get Carney's bird back.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:26.000
Maybe we should put out an APB.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.000
Why the cue?

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.000
This is not fun and games time, Eve.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:33.000
It all ties in.

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.000
It does?

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.000
Yeah, I give you Horatio Schuett,

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:40.000
I give you Alfred Carney, and I give you Robert Ironside.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.000
Now, what do we have in common?

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.000
Violence. Schuett was murdered, Carney was beaten,

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.000
and your office was bugged.

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:49.000
The common denominator behind the violence?

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:52.000
At one time or another, each one of you had that bird.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.000
And now McKay comes in and wants it.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:57.000
And as of this moment, seated in this chair, in this office,

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:00.000
at this point in time, what do I want?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.000
To know what that bird knows.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.000
Uh...

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Hi, sweetie. What do you say, Mac?

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:10.000
Ooga, ooga, ooga, ooga!

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Yes? This is Elda Thompson with the Herald of Hope magazine.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.000
No, he's very busy today.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.000
Perhaps you could call back later in the week.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
Ha!

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:37.000
Who was that?

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.000
A woman reporter. I told her to call back.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.000
Good.

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:43.000
He sure is hooked on these grapes.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.000
Whistle for the doggie.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.000
He's hooked on any fruit that's soft enough.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:50.000
These birds are always hungry.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.000
As long as you feed him, he keeps talking.

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:54.000
So it seems.

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:57.000
That seems to be the extent of his vocabulary.

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:59.000
Whistle for the doggie and fly the cue.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.000
Fly the cue? Is he trying to say fly the coop?

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Possibly.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.000
Fly the cue.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.000
Cue.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.000
How many words sound like cue?

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.000
Well, there's cue like in a play.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.000
Dramatic.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.000
And there's cue, you know, a Chinese pigtail.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Cosmetic.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.000
Cue as in pool.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.000
Sporting.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.000
Aye.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:25.000
I don't think Mr. MacAbre's cue falls in any of those categories.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:30.000
All right, if it's not dramatic, cosmetic or sporting, where does it fall?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.000
I'd say...

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:35.000
Detentions...

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.000
And...

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
Correction.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.000
Fly the cue.

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.000
Hey.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.000
Big cue welcomes you, chief.

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.000
St. Quentin has been waiting for you with open arms.

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:49.000
I know a lot of people up here.

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:52.000
Wish I could say it was nice to see you again.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.000
If you'd said it, I wouldn't believe it.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.000
There you go again, being cynical.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:02.000
It must be awful not to have any faith in your fellow man.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.000
Sometimes it keeps me awake at night.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.000
See?

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:10.000
I sleep like a baby.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:13.000
Maybe what I need is a hobby.

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:15.000
You?

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:19.000
I thought your hobby was ripping up innocents, like me.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:23.000
True. I hear you've become Quentin's animal trainer.

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:25.000
Yeah.

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:29.000
I started with fleas, and I'm working my way up to elephants.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:32.000
Some guys paint, others carve, make belts, and I...

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:34.000
You train birds.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.000
Ah.

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:38.000
Ain't no law against it.

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:41.000
I mean, I need the breadth of my canteen fund.

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:46.000
Did you know that Connie McKay bought your last bird?

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:49.000
I'm not surprised. He buys lots of stuff the guys make up here.

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:52.000
Groms, what do you hear from Arnie Sims?

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:54.000
Hey, knock it off, chief.

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Can't you harp on anybody besides Sims?

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.000
You fuzz never give up, do you?

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:05.000
I never give up trying to understand what makes you a sucker.

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:10.000
You've been here two years waiting for a trip to the green room, and Arnie?

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:13.000
Arnie's on the outside having a ball.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:18.000
I don't know what you're talking about. I never knew Arnie Sims.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.000
And I never killed that guard.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:24.000
And you never heard of an armored truck?

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:27.000
And you never heard of $250,000?

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:33.000
We were never able to tie Sims in with Groms on that heist in murdering that guard.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:37.000
What would make you think we could do it now?

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:41.000
I appreciate that editorial wee.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:45.000
Well, maybe the royal wee is rubbed off.

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:50.000
Ed, a good cop learns from his mistakes.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:55.000
Up to now, I always figured that after the heist, Sims took the money.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:58.000
Yes.

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:08.000
You may find this hard to believe, but there is a remote possibility that I may have been mistaken.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:12.000
In the time you've had him, what have you taught him to say?

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:15.000
Nothing new. That takes a while.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:19.000
And he could already say the things he says now when you got him from McKay's pet store?

00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:25.000
Yes, sir. But I did teach him to imitate an auto horn.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:28.000
We noticed.

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:32.000
What are you going to do with me now that I'm up and around?

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:35.000
Going to put me in another prison?

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:39.000
Going to put me in another prison?

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:42.000
You didn't really kill Horatio, did you?

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:43.000
Of course I didn't.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:47.000
Well, then you're free, Carney.

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:52.000
After all those years, you're finally free.

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:53.000
To do what?

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:58.000
Oh, anything. You are your own man.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:02.000
Thank you.

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:03.000
Where would I go?

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:08.000
There's a whole world waiting for you.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:09.000
That's what you wanted, isn't it?

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Yes. Yes, of course. Except...

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
What about the house?

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:18.000
Chute's house? Your prison?

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:25.000
It would be a place to stay. For a while.

00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:32.000
Perhaps I could fix it with the executor of the estate. For a while.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:37.000
Yes, yes, yes, just for a while.

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.000
Goodbye, Carney.

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:42.000
Goodbye, sweetie.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.000
Couldn't I take him with me?

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:48.000
No, I'm afraid not. We're keeping him for a few days.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:59.000
Mark?

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Do you think he's going to be all right alone?

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:12.000
Mark, no man is ever alone.

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:14.000
Chief, she's here now, in person.

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:16.000
The reporter who's been calling for an interview.

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:20.000
I'll say this for her, she's persistent and pretty, too.

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:26.000
Miss Whitfield, one of your more important jobs is to protect me from unnecessary interruptions.

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:30.000
Tell her I'm busy.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.000
Hi, sweetie.

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:42.000
Just a minute, Eve.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.000
You think she's a pretty girl?

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:48.000
Quite pretty.

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:54.000
On the other hand, when have we ever neglected our friends of the fourth estate?

00:29:54.000 --> 00:30:01.000
Bring her in.

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Won't you come in?

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.000
Thank you.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:10.000
This is Elda Thompson, Chief. She's from the Herald of Hope Magazine.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:12.000
Won't you sit down, Miss Thompson?

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:23.000
Thank you.

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:30.000
Well, as you probably know, our magazine is published by the Northeastern Orthopedic Foundation.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.000
We'd like to do a story on you.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:35.000
Most flattering. But why me?

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:40.000
Because you are an outstanding example of will triumphing over a handicap.

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:43.000
I assume my good friend, Dr. Wright, put you up to this.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.000
The president of the foundation.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
And how is Dr. Cummings?

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:50.000
His assistant. Well, he's not with us anymore.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:53.000
He's doing research in Australia.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:56.000
Yes, I believe I did read that somewhere.

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:59.000
Well, we might as well get started.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Well, I'm not really prepared to. I just wanted to make an appointment.

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Well, then, how about tomorrow?

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:09.000
That would be fine.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:11.000
Ten o'clock in the morning?

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:15.000
Yes.

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:20.000
Hi, sweetie. Fly the queue.

00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:22.000
I see you keep a parrot.

00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Parrot? Hardly.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:27.000
That's an ugly banana-eating cousin of a crow.

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.000
I think he's beautiful.

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:31.000
See you tomorrow, Miss Thompson.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:36.000
Thank you.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.000
Hi.

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:41.000
Thank you.

00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:43.000
Here it is, Chief.

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:46.000
Thanks.

00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:52.000
All right. Let's start the floor show.

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Assume Grom's in prison.

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:58.000
Knows where he stashed the loot from the armored car robbery.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:01.000
Arnie Simms free on the outside, doesn't.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:04.000
Grom, whose cut might keep him out of the gas chamber,

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.000
had to get the information out to Simms.

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:09.000
On death row, correspondence is a little difficult.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:11.000
Right. So, be it.

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Being a creative fellow, Grom's got a feathered carrier,

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:16.000
but not the pigeon.

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:18.000
Mr. Macabre.

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:19.000
Fly the queue.

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:21.000
That's right.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:23.000
But a car accident put Simms in the hospital.

00:32:23.000 --> 00:32:25.000
And Carney got the bird.

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:27.000
Hi, sweetie.

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:29.000
Simms found out who had Mr. Macabre.

00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:32.000
He broke into the house, shoot surprised him, and was killed.

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
Fly the queue.

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.000
Fly the queue.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
That's Grom's appeal for help.

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:42.000
To fly the queue means to get out of San Quentin.

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:44.000
Whistle for the doggie.

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.000
Whistle for the doggie.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:47.000
Is he telling us to do something?

00:32:47.000 --> 00:32:48.000
I doubt it.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:49.000
Why?

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.000
For one thing, we don't have a doggie.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:53.000
He could be telling us to get something.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:54.000
A whistle, maybe?

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.000
Sure, one of those little doggie whistles.

00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:59.000
The kind that only dogs can hear.

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:01.000
Supersonic.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Makes the kind of sound reproduced by a high tweeter.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.000
High tweeter, high whistle.

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:09.000
High tweeter, high tweeter, high tweeter.

00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:16.000
Mr. Macabre was calling for a whistle like this one.

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:40.000
Now for the moment of truth.

00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:49.000
Well, you can't win them all.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:51.000
Ding dong bell.

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:53.000
Ding dong bell.

00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:57.000
There's a giant step.

00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:04.000
Ding dong bell.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:05.000
Pussies in the well.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
Precisely.

00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:10.000
Mr. Macabre, with an assist from Officer Whitfield,

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:13.000
has told us where Groms hid the money.

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.000
Ed, I want a list of all the business properties

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:18.000
in the three-block area of the scene of that armored car robbery.

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:21.000
I'll have it for you yesterday.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:22.000
A bird in the hand.

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:24.000
Is worth two in a bush.

00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:25.000
Wrong.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:28.000
This bird is worth $250,000.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:51.000
Good morning, Chief.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:52.000
Ma.

00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:53.000
Morning, Eve.

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:55.000
This hat box came for you this morning.

00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:57.000
For me, here at headquarters?

00:34:57.000 --> 00:34:59.000
Yes, perhaps you have a secret admirer

00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:01.000
who doesn't know where you live.

00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:02.000
We listened to it, didn't tick.

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:04.000
It's not a bomb.

00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:06.000
Oh, good grief.

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:07.000
I take it back.

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:10.000
It is a bomb.

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:11.000
Oh, this is ridiculous.

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:18.000
It's built to me.

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:20.000
Hello, this is Eve Whitfield.

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:23.000
I just received a hat.

00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:25.000
No, I didn't order it.

00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.000
And if I wanted to wear a hat,

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.000
I certainly wouldn't wear that one, I assure you.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:30.000
Tell him, tiger.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.000
She's not going to pay for it,

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:33.000
and they can pick it up at any time.

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.000
No, I will not pay for it.

00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:37.000
And you can pick it up at your convenience.

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:43.000
Yes, that's my final word.

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Minority opinion acknowledged.

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:47.000
Mr. McCobber thinks you should keep it.

00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:50.000
Well, he can have it for a nest, as far as I'm concerned.

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:52.000
I don't know how they can make such a mistake.

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:54.000
I'm not sure it is a mistake, Eve.

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
They shouldn't be all surprised.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:57.000
Oh, hello, Miss Thompson.

00:35:57.000 --> 00:36:01.000
Mark, you've been waiting to work on the engine of the paddy wagon.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:04.000
Is it going to take an hour just to tell me I can't just walk?

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:05.000
You've got an hour, one hour.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:06.000
Good morning, Miss Thompson.

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:07.000
Come in, come in.

00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:09.000
Please have a chair.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:15.000
Thank you.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.000
You're very giving me a start.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:18.000
He'll do that.

00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:21.000
Perhaps we could do it without his comments, Eve.

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:24.000
You're hardly my idea of a medical writer.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:26.000
Nice of you to say that, Chief Ironside.

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.000
Actually, I'm not.

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:31.000
We have doctors who act as consultants for our staff.

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:32.000
I see.

00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:34.000
Well, now, I've jotted down a few questions.

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:35.000
Shall we get started?

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Just a moment, please.

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:40.000
Eve, I think you'd better go downstairs and review the Carter case.

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.000
The Carter case?

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:43.000
That's right. Remember the Carter case?

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.000
Yes, of course.

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:48.000
It's a matter of procedure.

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:50.000
Right, Chief.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:57.000
Now, Miss Thompson, you were probably interested in criminal investigation with the medical slant, right?

00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:59.000
Exactly.

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:02.000
Oh, I can tell this is going to be a very efficient interview.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:04.000
We hope so, Miss Thompson.

00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:09.000
Now, a case that comes to mind in that regard happened a couple of years ago.

00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:11.000
The newspapers covered it quite well.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:15.000
Matter of fact, I can probably save you a great deal of time by breaking out my files.

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:17.000
They're in the next room, if you'll excuse me.

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:20.000
Of course.

00:37:48.000 --> 00:38:05.000
Well, it took me a moment to locate it.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:09.000
Sorry.

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:12.000
You'll find some of my personal notes in there,

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:16.000
and perhaps I can add a few personal observations to spice up your story.

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Wonderful.

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:24.000
Oh, this is exactly what I've been looking for.

00:38:24.000 --> 00:38:26.000
How perceptive of you to hit it on it immediately.

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:29.000
We try. Feel free to ask.

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:30.000
I'm from Dorton's.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.000
Supposed to pick up a hat here for a Mrs. Whitefield or something like that.

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:37.000
A Miss Switfield. Here it is.

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:38.000
Thank you.

00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:40.000
You're welcome.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:54.000
All right, Miss Thompson, let's get on with it.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.000
Thank you, sir.

00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:00.000
I had no idea you kept such meticulous files.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:04.000
All I have to do is study them and abstract the material I need for the article.

00:39:04.000 --> 00:39:07.000
There's no need to waste any more of your valuable time, Chief Ironside.

00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:09.000
But it's a pleasure, Miss Thompson.

00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:11.000
Well, thank you. Thank you, Gann.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:13.000
I'll call you for another appointment.

00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:38.000
Of course.

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:40.000
What are you doing here?

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:43.000
I brought you the file on the Carter case.

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:51.000
Look in the cage.

00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:53.000
Why that dirty birdnapper?

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
She didn't take it. The messenger did.

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:56.000
I never did trust her.

00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:57.000
Neither did I.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:40:01.000
Well, then why did you send me out to look up a case that's been closed for two years?

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:03.000
What was the Carter case?

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:06.000
Well, there was this lady newspaper photographer.

00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.000
She stole this actress's Pekingese.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:19.000
I waited in the lobby for her, and I followed.

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:21.000
Hi, sweetie.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.000
I think you're cute, too.

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:27.000
But tell us, where is all that beautiful money?

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:28.000
Why the cue?

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.000
Now, that I dig.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.000
Groms wants to blow the cue scene.

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:36.000
What's with that whistle for the doggy bit?

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:38.000
Whistle for the doggy.

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:40.000
You're a big help, baby.

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:43.000
To you, too, sweetheart.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:47.000
Oh, and I think how we knocked ourselves out to get that buzzard.

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.000
Shut up, Elder.

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:49.000
I don't know.

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.000
I just want to tell her something.

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:53.000
Listen, I have news for you, honey.

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:55.000
This whole ball of wax is just to put on.

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:56.000
Forget it.

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:58.000
Let him buy his own fruit.

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:12.000
Don't shut up, Elder.

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:21.000
Cool it, I'm coming.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:22.000
Hi, honey.

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:23.000
Long time.

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:24.000
How'd you find me?

00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.000
You hiding out?

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:27.000
I didn't know I wasn't supposed to find you.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:30.000
I didn't know there was an Arnie Simms Sleeps Here sign in the front of the building, either.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.000
Well, your friends can always find you if they really want to.

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:35.000
What made you want to find me?

00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:37.000
A little bird.

00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:51.000
A little black bird.

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:53.000
I don't know what you're talking about, baby.

00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:55.000
Come off it, will you, Arnie?

00:41:55.000 --> 00:42:00.000
I come here to help you out.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.000
What do you mean, to help?

00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:03.000
I had that bird in my shop for three weeks.

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:05.000
His patter really cut a groove in my brain.

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:12.000
So, uh, how you gonna help me?

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:18.000
You want to find out where Gromes hid that money?

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:22.000
We're partners.

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:26.000
Bring the bird out here.

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:37.000
Some days you can almost make a buck out of that pet shop.

00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:38.000
Here's the list of properties.

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:41.000
The ones around the robbery site.

00:42:41.000 --> 00:42:43.000
All these places were closed.

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:45.000
Right.

00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:47.000
They've been closed since the day of the heist.

00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:48.000
Yes, sir.

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.000
And they're all within ten minutes of the robbery.

00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:56.000
Good. Spencer Motel, Delight Delicatessen, W&amp;W Electric.

00:42:56.000 --> 00:42:58.000
Epui Restaurant.

00:42:58.000 --> 00:42:59.000
Epui.

00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:08.000
That means the well in French.

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:10.000
Sure doesn't look like much.

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:13.000
Yeah, it was prettier in Fort Knox.

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:18.000
Gromes and I used to get smashed there plenty of times before they closed it down.

00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:21.000
I had to get off the street.

00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:20.000
You see anything?

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Hang onto me, McKay.

00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:23.000
Wait.

00:44:23.000 --> 00:44:24.000
Ooh.

00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:25.000
Wait.

00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:26.000
Oh.

00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:27.000
Drop it, Tims.

00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:28.000
Put up your hands.

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:29.000
You too, McKay.

00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:58.000
Shh.

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:11.520
Well, Miss Thompson, you really have a story now.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:13.920
Why did you ask me to meet you here?

00:45:13.920 --> 00:45:17.440
I thought you'd want to know where you caught the man who murdered Mr. Shue.

00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:18.440
He did?

00:45:18.440 --> 00:45:22.840
Well, that doesn't bring him back, does it?

00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:27.920
Perhaps you'd be interested to learn that your favorite pet shop owner was also in on

00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:28.920
this.

00:45:28.920 --> 00:45:29.920
He's in jail.

00:45:29.920 --> 00:45:30.920
Mr. McKay?

00:45:30.920 --> 00:45:34.000
Oh, that's too bad.

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:37.040
Too bad for all the little creatures shut up in these cages.

00:45:37.040 --> 00:45:38.520
They sure make a racket.

00:45:38.520 --> 00:45:41.120
Well, they must be hungry.

00:45:41.120 --> 00:45:43.400
Oh, yes, look.

00:45:43.400 --> 00:45:44.400
And they're thirsty.

00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:47.400
Oh, look at these cages here.

00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:52.640
Well, I don't think they've been cleaned in a week.

00:45:52.640 --> 00:45:56.240
As I was saying, too bad that McKay's in jail.

00:45:56.240 --> 00:46:00.240
Yes, that's right.

00:46:00.240 --> 00:46:02.240
What's going to happen to them?

00:46:02.240 --> 00:46:03.240
To whom?

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:08.440
What do all these little creatures that shut up in these cages?

00:46:08.440 --> 00:46:09.800
I have no idea.

00:46:09.800 --> 00:46:15.040
Well, somebody's got to take care of them and feed them and give them water and pet

00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:18.480
them so that they'll be happy, won't you?

00:46:18.480 --> 00:46:20.480
Well, I could do it.

00:46:20.480 --> 00:46:24.880
You could just get a caretaker to stay in Mr. Shue's house.

00:46:24.880 --> 00:46:31.640
Well, I think I might get McKay's attorney to make you custodian of the shop for the

00:46:31.640 --> 00:46:32.640
time being.

00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:33.640
You could.

00:46:33.640 --> 00:46:41.080
Ed, give Mr. Kearney the keys.

00:46:41.080 --> 00:46:45.400
Mr. Kearney, there's something else you should know.

00:46:45.400 --> 00:46:48.880
Mr. Shue remembered you in his will.

00:46:48.880 --> 00:46:55.880
Mr. Kearney, Mr. Shute left you $10,000.

00:46:55.880 --> 00:46:56.880
$10,000?

00:46:56.880 --> 00:46:57.880
Almost $10,000.

00:46:57.880 --> 00:47:03.840
I could buy the shop.

00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:08.520
Couldn't I?

00:47:08.520 --> 00:47:16.280
It's your money.

00:47:16.280 --> 00:47:23.640
Could I keep Mr. McCarver now?

00:47:23.640 --> 00:47:24.640
Of course.

00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:25.640
Whistle for the doggy.

00:47:25.640 --> 00:47:28.160
Of course, it would be a great blow to my staff.

00:47:28.160 --> 00:47:30.840
But we'll make the sacrifice.

00:47:30.840 --> 00:47:34.040
Thank you, Giant Mark.

00:47:34.040 --> 00:47:39.280
You have the keys.

00:47:39.280 --> 00:47:40.280
See you around, Bert.

00:47:40.280 --> 00:48:00.060
祝你成功.

00:48:00.060 --> 00:48:05.060
